{"sections":[{"_id":"6a55e4e91cf65a6171057917","name":"Default section","displayOrder":1,"isOptional":false,"questions":[{"_id":"6a55e4ec1cf65a6171057962","type":"Notebook","questionNumber":1,"positiveMarks":4,"positiveMarksStr":"4","negativeMarks":1,"negativeMarksStr":"1","partialPositiveMarks":null,"partialPositiveMarksStr":null,"texts":null,"imageIds":{"en":{"_id":"6a55e4eab3821e35efb5ba49","name":"QUES_ENG_3ejr8gncgp9vu87auiflrgive.png","baseUrl":"https://static.pw.live/","key":"5b09189f7285894d9130ccd0/1dc61f38-2069-481d-b8e3-054ad4dcebea.png"}},"options":[],"difficultyLevel":2,"pyqYears":[],"topicId":{"name":"Cell Organelles","_id":"6ucab1iqh8p30y0ludqaybfky"},"sectionId":"6a55e4e91cf65a6171057917","subjectId":"2tzgmg3pq30fcncg3tgdqqanc","chapterId":"1fmlbtl4vg36eyodau0l1vtnt","solutions":[],"solutionText":"0","solutionDescription":[{"_id":"6a7037d2425de6c9f46ea409","texts":{"en":"(i) Cell membrane and Cell wall (permeability)\nCell membrane: Selectively permeable (controls what enters and exits).\n\nCell wall: Freely permeable (allows most substances to pass through).\n\n\n\n\n(ii) RER and SER (structure)\nRER (Rough Endoplasmic Reticulum): Has ribosomes attached to its surface, giving it a rough appearance.\n\nSER (Smooth Endoplasmic Reticulum): Lacks ribosomes on its surface, giving it a smooth appearance.\n\n\n\n\n(iii) Chloroplasts and Chromoplasts (pigments)\nChloroplasts: Contain the green pigment chlorophyll (essential for photosynthesis).\n\nChromoplasts: Contain non-green colored pigments (like carotenoids, giving yellow, orange, or red colors to flowers and fruits)"},"videos":{"en":{"videoType":"penpencilvdo","videoUrl":"https://d1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net/254f1e80-6d77-43e5-b2c0-1c4aea4ee6c1/master.mpd"}},"videoType":"penpencilvdo","videoDetails":{"_id":"6a438638a166b8887ca93c11","id":"6a438638a166b8887ca93c11","name":"Copy of Q (1).mp4","image":"","videoUrl":"https://d1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net/254f1e80-6d77-43e5-b2c0-1c4aea4ee6c1/master.mpd",